# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large binaries. The working tree is ~18 GB; ~9.4 GB of that is weights and
# per-run archives, every individual file of which is ~1 GB and therefore over
# GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# Excluding them is safe for reproducibility: every diagnostic in scripts/
# re-derives its numbers from results/*.json and the per-run
# ablation_*.json, all of which ARE versioned. See AGENTS.md, "File map".
#
# NOTE (AGENTS.md, "Transcribe the verdict"): each run's pruned_ocr_results.zip
# holds the *executed* __notebook__.ipynb, which is the only place the printed
# Q1-Q6 verdicts live. Those zips are ~970 MB each and cannot be versioned here.
# If a verdict log needs to be public, extract the notebook out of the zip and
# commit that file on its own -- the pattern already used for
# `run 12/_cell15.txt`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.bin
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caches, editor and agent-harness state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.virtual_documents/
.claude/
.kilo/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebook/tracker backups written by the asserted patchers. Regenerable:
# kaggle_pruning_run.ipynb comes from scripts/make_kaggle_pruning_notebook.py,
# and the patchers refuse to overwrite an existing backup. Keeping them out of
# history avoids shipping eight near-identical multi-MB notebooks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak-*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENSED CORPUS DATA -- added 2026-10-03, before the official SROIE download.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. ICDAR RRC data is obtained under the competition's
# own terms, which this project has not yet read and which may forbid
# redistribution. Republishing it from here would be an irreversible disclosure,
# so the guard goes in BEFORE the data arrives rather than after.
#
# Note *.jpg/*.png are NOT globally excluded (visualizations/ and
# sample_document.png are deliberately versioned), so a `git add -A` over a
# downloaded corpus directory WOULD have committed it. These rules are
# directory-scoped for that reason.
#
# If the terms turn out to permit redistribution, remove these lines
# deliberately and say so in AGENTS.md -- do not let data arrive in history as
# a side effect of a bulk add.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
corpora/
# Any path containing SROIE, at any depth, file or directory. Verified 2026-10-03
# that `git ls-files | grep -i sroie` is EMPTY, so this broad rule shadows no
# tracked file. It is deliberately broad: the narrower list below missed
# `SROIE2019/` -- the actual extraction directory of the real download -- which
# `git check-ignore` reported as NOT IGNORED. A guard that misses the real case
# is the only kind that matters.
*SROIE*
*sroie*
sroie_official/
ICDAR2019*/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEGATIONS added 2026-10-04 -- the rules above were swallowing the project's OWN
# analysis code and its evidence. Measured in Project-kilo: `*sroie*` IGNORED
# `scripts/verify_official_sroie.py` (PATCH J's companion verifier, 26/26) AND
# `results/_v_official_sroie.log` (the only evidence that it ran), and
# `git ls-files --error-unmatch` confirmed BOTH untracked. Committing that stream
# as-is would have silently dropped a verifier and its log out of the repo --
# which is what claim 4 (the methodological layer) rests on.
#
# Why the original check missed it, and both halves are this project's own
# documented patterns:
#   * `git ls-files | grep -i sroie` was EMPTY on 2026-10-03 and that was TRUE --
#     the verifier was written on 2026-10-04. A guard validated against the tree
#     as it stood is invalidated by the next file anyone adds.
#   * the "must-not-ignore control" used `scripts/verify_corpus_grain.py`, whose
#     name contains no "sroie" -- i.e. a control drawn from OUTSIDE the rule's
#     domain, which could not have failed. Decorative by construction.
#
# These two lines re-include CODE and LOGS only, never data. Verified in a scratch
# repo: verifier + log TRACKABLE, while `sroie_official/sub/X1.jpg` and
# `SROIE2019-*.zip` stay IGNORED. Note a negation cannot rescue anything under an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so `sroie_official/` above is unaffected by these.
# ⚠ `_v_official_sroie.log` quotes a handful of GT transcription fragments as
# evidence (e.g. one cp1252 line). That is quotation, not redistribution -- but it
# is a deliberate choice, recorded here so it can be overruled.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!scripts/*sroie*.py
!results/*sroie*.log
*task1train*/
*task2train*/
*task3train*/
*task1_2-test*/
*/0325updated*
# Belt and braces: HF datasets cache, if anyone points HF_HOME into the repo.
.cache/
huggingface/

